------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  THE PREMISE K07-B DOES NOT STATE.  The derivation fixes g_bar and g_obs at ONE point.  An estimator that
    fits the SHAPE of a whole curve with the normalisation of g_bar free is outside its scope.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    K07-B's own wording is 'for any estimator that reads a_0 off a measured pair (g_bar, g_obs) through the
    kernel' -- which is the pointwise class -- but the CONCLUSION it draws is unrestricted: 'removing Upsilon
    cannot help, because it moves leverage to the hydrogen mass scale one for one.'  Section 3 measures that.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.  BOTH ESTIMATORS, BOTH SETS OF LEVERS, MEASURED BY BRUTE FORCE ON THE SAME 40 SPARC GALAXIES.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    sample: 40 galaxies (K07-A's pre-declared Upsilon-free cut)
    shape-marginalised estimator (K07-A) : a_0 = 1.3139e-10
    pointwise inversion at Upsilon = 0.5 : a_0 = 1.3991e-10  on 481 points with y < 0.3, median Phi = 0.5769  ->  theorem predicts SUM = -1.363

  lever (measured by re-running the whole estimator at x1.25 and x0.80)   shape (K07-A)   pointwise
  d log a_0 / d log Upsilon  (stellar mass scale)                              0.000      -1.322
  d log a_0 / d log M_gas    (hydrogen mass scale)                            -0.421      -0.286
  d log a_0 / d log D        (distance scale)                                 -1.421      -2.567
  SUM of the two baryon levers  (K07-B says this is -Phi/(1-Phi), |.| >= 1)          -0.421      -1.608
  K07-B prediction at the measured median Phi                                             -1.363
  [PASS] B3 THE THEOREM IS CONFIRMED WHERE IT APPLIES: for the pointwise estimator the two baryon levers sum to the predicted -Phi/(1-Phi), measured by brute force rather than derived   (measured SUM = -1.608 against the predicted -1.363 at the sample's median Phi = 0.5769 (18% agreement; the residual is the spread of Phi over the points, since the median of a nonlinear function is not the function of the median))
  [PASS] B4 AND K07-B'S HEADLINE CONCLUSION IS FALSE, contradicted from inside its own batch of candidates. K07-B says removing Upsilon 'moves leverage to the hydrogen mass scale one for one' so the total can never go below 1. K07-A's shape-marginalised estimator, run here on the same 40 galaxies, has a stellar lever of exactly zero and a gas lever well under 1, so its TOTAL calibration leverage is less than half the floor K07-B declares unbreachable. The theorem is true; the sentence drawn from it is not, because a shape fit is not a pointwise inversion   (shape estimator total baryon leverage |-0.421| against K07-B's floor of 1 and against the pointwise estimator's own measured -1.608 on the same galaxies)

    WHAT THIS BUYS, in the currency the programme actually needs (item 123: 3 sigma between the footings is
    0.0273 dex in a_0), assuming the calibration in question is the only error:
    estimator                     |lever| on Upsilon  |lever| on M_gas  Upsilon needed  M_gas needed
    shape-marginalised (K07-A)                 0.000             0.421           exact         16.1%
    pointwise inversion                        1.322             0.286            4.9%         24.6%
  [PASS] B5 THE CONSEQUENCE, and it is a correction to the standing ledger's costing: the veins ledger records that every route dropping the stellar M/L 'picks up the HI mass scale at lever -1.11', which would put a 3 sigma footing decision behind a 5.8% hydrogen mass scale. Measured here on the same survey, the shape estimator's TOTAL baryon leverage is 3.8x smaller than the pointwise estimator's, and its gas lever is -0.42, not -1.11 -- so the same decision needs the hydrogen scale only to 16%, not 6%   (total baryon leverage 0.421 (shape) vs 1.608 (pointwise), a factor 3.8; 3 sigma needs M_gas to 16.1% here against the ledger's 5.8% at lever -1.11, and to 24.6% through the pointwise route whose leverage sits on Upsilon (-1.322) instead)

  [PASS] B6 AGAINST BOTH CANDIDATES: neither K07-B's conservation law nor K07-A's zero lever says anything about the DISTANCE scale, and the distance lever measured here is the largest of the three for the shape estimator too. A lever budget that contains only Upsilon and gas is not the error budget   (shape estimator: d log a_0/d log D = -1.421 against a gas lever of -0.421 and a stellar lever of +0.000; pointwise: -2.567)

